Z||000003||Formula88||12-13-2001||09:58 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by NIFE [PaulV]:<BR><B> All 304 aircraft quality stainless system with Borla tips installed has a million mile warranty! This system will be the last system you will ever need to buy for your Fiero! </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>But the Fiero OEM exhaust is stainless steel, too.  Why wouldn't it be the last system I'll ever need to buy for my Fiero?!?!?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Do you happen to know offhand what the pipe dimensions on that system are?  Thanks.||||reg||12
Z||000004||pherder||12-13-2001||10:15 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR><B> But the Fiero OEM exhaust is stainless steel, too.  Why wouldn't it be the last system I'll ever need to buy for my Fiero?!?!?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Do you happen to know offhand what the pipe dimensions on that system are?  Thanks.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The reason it should be the last system you buy is Borla's Million mile warrantee!  GM didn't have that kind of warrantee.<P>Second question answer ... if it is the same as the first batch (sold by Tim), I have one and it is 2" diameter.<P>Paul<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroRacer||12-13-2001||05:14 PM||||Not to mention the Borla system uses Mandrel Bends which the stock system doesn't.  Less restriction.  Isn't the stock system 2" also?||||reg||1
Z||000006||NIFE [PaulV]||12-13-2001||08:58 PM||||The Borla system has a 2" pipe, same as it had during its first run of production. About the only change is that Bob will weld on one of the hangar brackets before he ships to make a DIY install easier.||||reg||1
